# The upstream reader

### `apps/reader` and the packages under it

Tutors Ladder, Reader (rung 4), talk 3. Every path is at tutors-mono-repo `2b96b69`.

---

## `apps/reader`, top level

```
apps/reader/
  package.json          svelte 5.57.2, @sveltejs/kit 3.1.1, "#lib/*": "./src/lib/*"
  vite.config.ts        createViteConfig from @tutors/app-config
  playwright.config.ts, playwright.static.config.ts
  src/
    app.css  app.html  hooks.client.ts  hooks.server.ts
    lib/                actor-data.ts  root-data.ts  server/
    routes/
  tests/e2e/            reading, resource-cards, accessibility, static-reader, ...
```

The app is thin. Almost every component lives in `packages/svelte/*`.

---

## The route groups

| Group or folder | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `(course-reader)/` | `course`, `topic`, `lab`, `note`, `talk`, `video`, `wall`, `search`, `quiz`, `notebook`, `whiteboard`, ... |
| `(home)/` | the home page and the course list |
| `(auth)/` | sign-in pages |
| `(create)/` | the course creation wizard and check page |
| `api/`, `healthz/`, `metrics/`, `version/` | `+server.ts` endpoints |

Rung 4 mirrors `(course-reader)` with four kinds of page, and none of the endpoints.

---

## How a course page is built

`docs/COURSE-PAGE-WALKTHROUGH.md`, section 6:

| Route | Service method | Component |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/course/[courseid]` | `readCourse` | `structure/Composite.svelte` |
| `/topic/[courseid]/[...loid]` | `readTopic` | `structure/Composite.svelte` |
| `/lab/[courseid]/[...loid]` | `readLab` | `content/lab/Lab.svelte` |
| `/note/[courseid]/[...loid]` | `readLo` | `content/Note.svelte` |
| `/talk/[courseid]/[...loid]` | `readLo` | `content/talk/TalkAdobe`, `TalkClient` or `TalkMarp` |

> Every learning-object route in the reader has the same shape: a route folder, a `courseService` method,
> an index lookup, and one component from `@tutors/ui-components`.

---

## Three UI packages, one direction

`ARCHITECTURE.md`: "The one-directional dependency flow is: `ui-components` -> `ui-navigators` ->
`ui-primitives`."

| Package | Holds (`packages/svelte/...`) |
| --- | --- |
| `ui-primitives` | `Icon`, `Image`, `Menu`, `Sidebar`, `StudentCard`, `utils/sanitize.ts` |
| `ui-navigators` | `TutorsShell`, `MainNavigator`, `SecondaryNavigator`, `footers/`, `search/` |
| `ui-components` | `learning-objects/layout`, `structure`, `content`; `quiz/`, `time/` |

Below them: `runes`, `course`, `themes`, `utils/i18n`, `utils/a11y` (ARCHITECTURE.md, "Layer Structure").

---

## The rule that keeps it

`.dependency-cruiser.cjs`, checked by `tests/architecture/dependency-rules.test.ts`:

```js
name: "ui-primitives-no-data-features",
comment: "UI primitives are low-level presentational components: they take users, events and
  permissions as props or context, and never reach into the data and access packages
  (community, connect, data-api, rbac) themselves. ...",
from: { path: "^packages/svelte/ui-primitives/" },
to:   { path: "^packages/svelte/(community|connect|data-api|utils/rbac)/" }
```

The same test proves `layer-ui-primitives`, `layer-ui-navigators` and `layer-ui-components` catch a
fixture that reaches up.

---

## The same rule, at rung 4

`tests/architecture/reader-layers.test.ts`

```ts
"lib/ui-primitives":  { may: [], kit: false, job: "... like upstream's ui-primitives they import no data" },
"lib/ui-navigators":  { may: ["lib/ui-primitives", "lib/runes", "lib/course"], kit: true, ... },
"lib/ui-components":  { may: ["lib/ui-navigators", "lib/ui-primitives", "lib/runes", "lib/course"], ... },
```

Folders, not packages: a learner reads one app. The direction is upstream's; the failure message names
the rule, the file and the fix.

---

## Themes

`packages/svelte/themes/src/services/themes.svelte.ts`

```ts
themes: [ { name: "tutors", ... }, { name: "classic", ... }, { name: "dyslexia", ... },
          { name: "terminus", ... }, { name: "rose", ... }, { name: "cerberus", ... },
          { name: "easter", icons: EasterIcons } ],

setTheme(theme: string): void {
  ...
  document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", this.currentTheme.value);
  localStorage.theme = this.currentTheme.value;
```

A theme is a `data-theme` attribute and a CSS file that overrides tokens
(`themes/src/styles/dyslexia.css`). Rung 4 has light and dark tokens in `app.css` and no saved choice:
the fence forbids browser storage.

---

## Interface text (i18n)

`packages/svelte/utils/i18n/src/index.ts`

```ts
export const SUPPORTED_LOCALES = ["en", "fr", "de", "it", "es", "ga"] as const;
export const locale = rune<SupportedLocale>("en");

export function t(key: MessageKey): string {
  return messages[locale.value]?.[key] ?? messages.en[key] ?? key;
}
```

- `messages/en.ts` defines `MessageKey`; components call `t("shell.next")`.
- `locale` is a rune, so changing it re-renders every `t(...)`.
- Drift again: `ARCHITECTURE.md` says "EN, DE, ES, FR, IT"; the code has six, with Irish (`ga`).

---

## Accessibility

| What | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Skip link, `main#main-content` with `tabindex="-1"` | `ui-navigators/src/TutorsShell.svelte` |
| Focus to `#main-content` after each navigation | `apps/reader/src/routes/(course-reader)/+layout.svelte` |
| `aria-current="step"` in the lab's step list | `packages/svelte/course/src/course/services/live-lab.ts` |
| Arrow keys move between lab steps | `ui-components/.../content/lab/Lab.svelte` |
| `prefersReducedMotion` rune | `packages/svelte/utils/a11y/src/reduced-motion.svelte.ts` |
| axe checks, light and dark | `apps/reader/tests/e2e/accessibility.spec.ts` (`@axe-core/playwright`) |

Rung 4 keeps the first four, in the same places.

---

## Running it

From the repository root (`apps/reader/README.md`):

```bash
pnpm install
cp .env.example .env        # PUBLIC_ANON_MODE=TRUE: no backend needed
pnpm dev                    # builds ui-primitives, ui-navigators, ui-components, then the reader
```

Then open <http://localhost:5173/course/reference-course>.

- Needs Node 26.13 or later (`package.json` `engines`, `.nvmrc`) and pnpm 11.24 or later.
- Edit a primitive and see no change? The UI packages ship built output; restart `pnpm dev`.

---

## What rung 4 leaves for later

| Upstream has | Arrives |
| --- | --- |
| `sanitizeHtml`, sign-in, roles, locks | rung 6 (Guarded) |
| BDD features, mutation testing | rung 5 (Proven) |
| `adapter-node`, the container, release gates | rung 7 (Shipped) |
| Tailwind, Skeleton, Iconify, markdown-it, Shiki, axe checks, presence, Supabase | the Summit |

Each line is a reason the rung 4 reader is 34 source files, where upstream's reader and the six packages
it draws pages from (`ui-*`, `course`, `runes`, `themes`) hold 238.

---

## What to take away

- `apps/reader` is routes; the UI is three packages in one direction.
- One rule in dependency-cruiser keeps primitives free of data; rung 4 keeps the same rule on folders.
- Themes are a `data-theme` attribute; text goes through `t(key)`; accessibility is in the shell and the
  layout, and checked by axe.
- Docs drift. Read the code, and note the drift: it is a good first contribution.
